    {
      "displayed": true,
      "end": 29,
      "ending": "Section4.6 continuous-test Riemann sums plus L3 UI identify every weak-measure subsequential limit as measurableH functional; ball indicators alone are insufficient. Deterministic smooth boundary has negligible mass. Quad-pivotal version discards boundary via side3arm/corner2arm, no uniform deterministic distance. Section4.7 enhanced tiling refinement gives reverse measure domination and nested Poisson samples; circular importance is bracketed, not declared identical. Section6 uses shifted/rotated grid averaging, Jacobian|gprime|^2 and arm ratio|fprime|^5/4 to obtain pivotal covariance|fprime|^3/4. No need for cluster/interface proof in this target.",
