      "ending": "Appendix D all read: L2 quasimultiplicativity uses conditional martingale Jensen for extension, an exact locality equality for the inner event, squared good/bad expansion with factor3, and weighted Lemma7.9 analogue. Local pivotal bounds expand a square and sum square roots of products of exponential density failures; this is how cells reaching across boundaries remain controlled under two replicas. Appendix A retains biased Fourier basis and factor1/[4p(1-p)] for monotone influences. Appendix B obtains whole-plane Poisson bounds via binomial coupling and an exploration of white clusters from the top boundary, whose revealment remains controlled when p>=1/2; it does not invoke unproved annealed BK at p>1/2. The nearcritical derivative step uses actual quenched influence counts and annealed pivotal bounds before integration. These operations supply static arm/replica controls, not a claim of a geometric dynamical limit.",
